#
# A logic:CompensationAttempt that binds NOTHING at all — the empty half of the
# exactness discipline. The charge it was raised to undo is right there in the scene,
# receipted and attributed to a real attempt, and the refund names none of it: read
# later, "a refund happened" is true and answers nothing about WHICH committed effect
# was counteracted, so the effect stays outstanding while the ledger reads as settled.
# MUST trip logic:CompensationNamesForwardEffectConstraint. NOT
# logic:CompensationBindsExactForwardEffectConstraint: that law DEREFERENCES the
# binding and its guard therefore binds it, so a compensation naming nothing falls
# outside it — the loose-binding case is compensation-outcome-without-receipt.ttl's
# sibling discipline and is exercised inline in crates/logic/tests/enactment_gate.rs.
# NOT logic:CompensationNotInverseConstraint either: the refund is not typed as the
# receipt it addresses, which is the separate prohibition
# compensation-typed-as-its-forward-receipt.ttl carries.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/logic/tests/> .

ex:invoice901Charge a logic:EffectAttempt ;
    rdfs:label "the charge dispatched against the payments provider"@en .

ex:invoice901ChargeReceipt a logic:ExternalEffectReceipt ;
    logic:receiptOfAttempt ex:invoice901Charge ;
    rdfs:label "the provider's receipt for the charge that committed"@en .

ex:invoice901Refund a logic:CompensationAttempt ;
    rdfs:label "a refund counteracting nothing nameable"@en .
